cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this computation or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "A22: validated interval replay of the full 128-pulse learning transient"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Breuillaud"
    given-names: "Nicolas"
version: "3.3"
date-released: "2026-10-22"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  End-to-end propagation of the A22 spiking-network realization (18 layers x 12 lanes,
  128 input pulses, horizon 1116) with outward-rounded affine interval arithmetic over a box of
  device parameters, independent for each input port of each cell, and initial states. All 18
  layers complete with no forced decision; the independent A14 reference gains lie inside the
  computed enclosures for 648 of 648 boxes. Experimental; not a qualified all-trajectories proof.
keywords:
  - interval arithmetic
  - affine arithmetic
  - hybrid systems
  - validated numerics
  - spiking networks
